    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="0362" n="246" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg246"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1451a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Chargé White.</hi><anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d330-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 29, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President will shortly propose a plan for the restoration of peace and
                    establishment of order in Santo Domingo. Meantime he asks that hostilities be
                    suspended until the proposition can be laid before Santo Domingo.</p>
                <pb facs="0363" n="247" xml:id="pg247"/>
                <p>Please communicate this to the Foreign Office and to all participants who can be
                    reached directly or indirectly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d330-f1" n="6" type="source" xml:id="d330-f1-content">
                <p>Same to American Consul at Puerto Plata.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
